From df042872da638d886a23b5534d9f4ea7e8cbfc19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 21:20:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(live): label serve switches & corrections in the
 spectator feed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Serve switches (side-out) and per-team corrections were broadcast through
point() as type:"point" with value 0 / -1, so the spectator feed rendered
nonsensical "Beta +0" / "Alpha +-1" rows. The scorer already tagged these
intents (kind:'serve'/'correction') but the broadcast dispatch dropped the tag.

Thread the event type end to end and render it:
- convex scorePoint: optional `type` arg (restricted to point|serve_change|
  correction), default "point"; runningA/runningB stay snapshot-authoritative
  and independent of type.
- useLiveBroadcast.point(): accepts/forwards `type` through the outbox; queued
  items without it default to point.
- MonoSetsLiveScore: dispatch maps intent.kind -> event type.
- MonoWatchMatch feed: serve_change -> "Serve -> {server}", correction ->
  "Correction · {team} -N"; point branch unchanged.

Pure labeling change: for an identical tap sequence the stored running totals
and reduced score are byte-identical (serve_change is a reduce no-op, correction
is the same signed adjustment value:-1 already was, score patches from snapshot).

Note: undo's target-scan still keys on type:"point" so it skips these events;
score stays correct (these occur only in snapshot-authoritative sports and undo
patches from the snapshot), only the compensating event's reversesSeq audit
metadata can reference the prior point. Cricket wickets (value:0 points) keep
"+0" — a separate cricket-specific concern.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
